# FitPlanCoach — reverse proxy for your EXISTING Caddy (coexists with OmniStack).
# Caddy provisions + renews HTTPS automatically once DNS points the domain here.
#
# FIRST find out whether your Caddy is a system service or a Docker container:
#   docker ps --format '{{.Names}} {{.Image}}' | grep -i caddy   # prints a line => Docker Caddy
#   systemctl is-active caddy                                     # "active"     => system Caddy
#
# Use the matching block below. Reloading Caddy is graceful — OmniStack stays up.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ============================================================
# CASE A — SYSTEM Caddy (a caddy service on the host)
# ============================================================
# The app is published on the host at 127.0.0.1:8080, so Caddy reaches it there.
# Append to /etc/caddy/Caddyfile, then:  sudo systemctl reload caddy
#
# fitplancoach.com, www.fitplancoach.com {
# 	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080
# }


# ============================================================
# CASE B — DOCKER Caddy (caddy runs as a container)  ← most common with OmniStack
# ============================================================
# IMPORTANT: inside the Caddy container, 127.0.0.1 is the CONTAINER, not the host,
# so 127.0.0.1:8080 will NOT work. Instead put both containers on one network and
# proxy to the container name + its INTERNAL port (3000). This is the #1 gotcha.
#
# 1) Find the network your Caddy container is on (replace caddy_container_name):
#      docker inspect -f '{{range $k,$v := .NetworkSettings.Networks}}{{$k}} {{end}}' caddy_container_name
# 2) Attach FitPlanCoach to that same network (no rebuild needed):
#      docker network connect <that_network> fitplancoach
# 3) Add this block to the Caddyfile your Caddy container uses, then reload it:
#      docker exec caddy_container_name caddy reload --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile
#
# fitplancoach.com, www.fitplancoach.com {
# 	reverse_proxy fitplancoach:3000
# }
#
# (container name = fitplancoach, internal port = 3000 — NOT 8080, NOT 127.0.0.1)
